    ('logical', 'one_shot', 'build_authoring', 'context_records', 'workflow.logical.common.build_authoring.inputs.context_records', 'json', 'Active Context records whose Context Type applies to this workflow, from active groups in authorized Project/Source System scope, are reusable guidance. Each record has context_record_id (canonical UUID), context_group_name, context_type_name, context_text and nullable source_reference. The type classifies its purpose; context_text contains the requirement, decision, rule, convention or other guidance, including relevant exceptions and acceptance criteria. source_reference records provenance. Use UUIDs for Context support references. Context applicability does not prove physical source data or replace measured validation; preserve registered lineage and distinguish guidance from observed evidence.', '[{"context_record_id":"90b6320b-c2e0-5e9d-bd00-0e14e6d259fe","context_group_name":"ERP relationship notes","context_type_name":"Business Requirement","context_text":"Within this ERP source, Orders.order_id identifies one order. Each order belongs to exactly one customer identified by Customers.customer_id through Orders.customer_id; one customer may have many orders. Customer IDs are stable within this source.","source_reference":"{\"section\": \"Orders and customers\"}"}]'::jsonb, 90),
    ('logical', 'one_shot', 'build_authoring', 'existing_entities', 'workflow.logical.common.build_authoring.inputs.existing_entities', 'json', 'Active Entities already built from this area''s tables, saved or built by an earlier area of this run, in the answer''s own compact language. Reuse and extend them; never create a second Entity for the same thing. List one in your answer only to change it. sources lists this area''s tables; other_source_count counts sources outside this area, which are kept. Generated keys and audit columns are not shown. relationships are links touching these Entities.', '{"entities":[{"schema":"silver","name":"SalesOrder","type":"transaction","definition":"One row per order a customer places.","grain":"One row per order_id.","is_locked":false,"sources":["t1"],"other_source_count":0,"attributes":[{"name":"CustomerID","type":"BIGINT","nullable":false,"natural_key":false,"from":["t1.customer_id"],"definition":"The Customer that placed this order.","is_locked":false}]}],"relationships":[{"from":{"schema":"silver","entity":"SalesOrder","attribute":"CustomerID"},"to":{"schema":"silver","entity":"Customer"},"cardinality":"many_to_one","basis":"Analysis: Orders.customer_id -> Customers.customer_id, supported.","is_locked":false}]}'::jsonb, 100),
