    ('dimensional', 'one_shot', 'build_authoring', 'object_relationship_context', 'workflow.dimensional.common.build_authoring.inputs.object_relationship_context', 'json', 'Read-only physical support traced from active lineage of the selected Logical Entities/Attributes; it does not expand Dimensional authoring sources. Existing applied relationships touching each scoped physical Object. Incoming matches the to-Object; outgoing matches the from-Object. Include empty groups. Preserve endpoint, hypothesis, lifecycle, lock and recorded validation fields. Validation outcome and aggregate counts are saved evidence, not a fresh measurement; all-null validation fields mean unvalidated. An endpoint outside object_context is contextual only and does not become an eligible authoring source.', '[{"tenant_code":"GDS","system_code":"WAREHOUSE","connection_code":"MAIN","object_schema":"bronze","object_name":"Orders","incoming_relationships":[],"outgoing_relationships":[{"from_tenant_code":"GDS","from_system_code":"WAREHOUSE","from_connection_code":"MAIN","from_object_schema":"bronze","from_object_name":"Orders","to_tenant_code":"GDS","to_system_code":"WAREHOUSE","to_connection_code":"MAIN","to_object_schema":"bronze","to_object_name":"Customers","from_attribute_name":"customer_id","to_attribute_name":"customer_id","relationship_kind":"reference","inferred_cardinality":"many_to_one","analysis_result_status":"active","analysis_result_is_locked":false,"validation_policy_version":"1.0.0","validation_result":"supported","validation_source_non_null_count":20,"validation_source_distinct_count":10,"validation_target_non_null_count":10,"validation_target_distinct_count":10,"validation_source_missing_target_count":0,"validation_unused_target_count":0,"validation_duplicate_target_key_count":0}]}]'::jsonb, 90),
    ('dimensional', 'one_shot', 'build_authoring', 'context_records', 'workflow.dimensional.common.build_authoring.inputs.context_records', 'json', 'Active Context records whose Context Type applies to this workflow, from active groups in authorized Project/Source System scope, are reusable guidance. Each record has context_record_id (canonical UUID), context_group_name, context_type_name, context_text and nullable source_reference. The type classifies its purpose; context_text contains the requirement, decision, rule, convention or other guidance, including relevant exceptions and acceptance criteria. source_reference records provenance. Use UUIDs for Context support references. Context applicability does not prove physical source data or replace measured validation; preserve registered lineage and distinguish guidance from observed evidence.', '[{"context_record_id":"9bbdef91-d027-58a3-b22f-92ef90293cd0","context_group_name":"Sales analytics rules","context_type_name":"Business Requirement","context_text":"One fact row represents one governed order. OrderCount is one for that row. Sum counts orders only across compatible aggregation levels.","source_reference":null}]'::jsonb, 100),
